IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla-damages`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_civil-liability-act-2002_baseline.py).
-- Expected results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenario au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake): Jake, 22, a delivery rider and contractor on an
-- e-bike, has his wrist broken by an opening car door on 12 April 2029 (k044). Whether the Motor Vehicle (Third Party
-- Insurance) Act 1943 applies (the door "a consequence of the driving", its s 3(7)) is asserted both ways. Amounts A, B and
-- C are the 2002-03 figures in ss 10(1) and 13(1), standing in for the year's gazetted amounts; the average weekly earnings
-- and the $20,000 assessment of the wrist are illustrative.

