§ `ss 3A, 5A -- which of Part 1A applies` -- k044 Jake both ways

#ASSERT `Which of Part 1A applies to my claim` `Jake doored on a delivery, the CTP Act applying` EQUALS `all of Part 1A: duty, causation, recreational activities, contributory negligence, obvious and inherent risk (ss 5B-5P)`
#ASSERT `Which of Part 1A applies to my claim` `Jake doored on a delivery, the door held not part of the driving` EQUALS `all of Part 1A: duty, causation, recreational activities, contributory negligence, obvious and inherent risk (ss 5B-5P)`
#ASSERT `Which of Part 1A applies to my claim` `a worker's common-law claim against the employer` EQUALS `none of Part 1A`
#ASSERT `Which of Part 1A applies to my claim` `an assault meant to injure` EQUALS `none of Part 1A`
#ASSERT `Which of Part 1A applies to my claim` `a smoker's claim against a tobacco company` EQUALS `only ss 5A-5D: the general duty and causation`
#ASSERT `Which of Part 1A applies to my claim` `a fall in a shop in June 2003` EQUALS `none of Part 1A`
#ASSERT `Which of Part 1A applies to my claim` `a disease of unknown start, symptoms first in 2005` EQUALS `all of Part 1A: duty, causation, recreational activities, contributory negligence, obvious and inherent risk (ss 5B-5P)`

§ `ss 3, 3A, 6 -- whose limits apply to my damages` -- k044 Jake both ways

#ASSERT `Which limits apply to my damages` `Jake doored on a delivery, the CTP Act applying` EQUALS `the limits in the Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943, not Part 2`
#ASSERT `Which limits apply to my damages` `Jake doored on a delivery, the door held not part of the driving` EQUALS `Part 2 of the Civil Liability Act: the general damages threshold, the earnings cap and the home care limits`
#ASSERT `Which limits apply to my damages` `a worker's common-law claim against the employer` EQUALS `the limits in Part 7 Division 2 of the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023, not Part 2`
#ASSERT `Which limits apply to my damages` `an assault meant to injure` EQUALS `none of Part 2's limits: the court may only refer to earlier awards (s 10A)`
#ASSERT `Which limits apply to my damages` `an injury on a domestic flight` EQUALS `none of Part 2: carriage by air`
#ASSERT `Which limits apply to my damages` `a fall in a shop in June 2003` EQUALS `Part 2 of the Civil Liability Act: the general damages threshold, the earnings cap and the home care limits`
#ASSERT `Which limits apply to my damages` `a fall in a shop in 2002` EQUALS `none of Part 2: the incident was before Part 2 commenced`
#ASSERT `Which limits apply to my damages` `a claim on a life insurance policy` EQUALS `none: not personal injury damages`

